# State-space block: a diagonal linear recurrence written out (s_t = decay * s_(t-1) + x_t B, y_t = s_t C) with a learned decay held in 0 to 1 by a sigmoid, so the sequence history lives in one fixed-size state instead of attention's growing key-value cache.
include "dense.mlpl";

def u:ssm_decay(a_logit) {
  "Per-dimension decay in (0, 1): sigmoid of the raw learned logit, so training can only slide it between forgetting and accumulating.";
  sigmoid(a_logit)
}

def u:ssm_scan(xB, decay, n, ds) {
  "The scan over n positions of the projected input xB [n, ds]: s_t = decay * s_(t-1) + xB_t, stacked as [n, ds]; sequential by construction (one repeat per position; the count traces through grad, finding F15; ds is passed because shape arithmetic is not traced, F11).";
  h = take(xB, 0, 0);
  out = reshape(h, [1, ds]);
  t = 1;
  steps = n - 1;
  repeat steps {
    h = decay * h + take(xB, 0, t);
    out = concat(out, reshape(h, [1, ds]), 0);
    t = t + 1
  };
  out
}

def u:ssm_states(x, a_logit, B, n, ds) {
  "The state at every position [n, ds] of an input x [n, dm]: project by B, then scan with the sigmoid decay.";
  u:ssm_scan(matmul(x, B), u:ssm_decay(a_logit), n, ds)
}

def u:ssm_out(x, a_logit, B, C, n, ds) {
  "The block output [n, dm]: every position's state read through C; the caller adds the residual.";
  matmul(u:ssm_states(x, a_logit, B, n, ds), C)
}

def u:ssm_params(dm, ds) {
  "Trainable parameters of the block: the decay logits, B [dm, ds], and C [ds, dm].";
  ds + dm * ds + ds * dm
}

def u:ssm_state_bytes(ds) {
  "Persistent sequence state at f64: one vector of ds values, whatever the history length.";
  ds * 8
}

def u:kv_bytes(history, dm) {
  "Persistent sequence state a one-head, one-layer causal attention keeps at f64: a key and a value row per token of history.";
  2 * history * dm * 8
}

def u:ssm_survival(decay, from_pos, to_pos) {
  "Mean over dimensions of the share of position from_pos's contribution still present in the state at to_pos: decay^(to_pos - from_pos), averaged.";
  mean(pow(decay, to_pos - from_pos))
}

def u:ssm_sel_scan(a, b, n, ds) {
  "Selective scan over n positions: s_t = a_t * s_(t-1) + b_t, where the decay a [n, ds] and the input b [n, ds] are both functions of the token; the stacked states [n, ds]. One repeat per position, as in the constant-decay scan (probe c1).";
  h = take(b, 0, 0);
  out = reshape(h, [1, ds]);
  t = 1;
  steps = n - 1;
  repeat steps {
    h = take(a, 0, t) * h + take(b, 0, t);
    out = concat(out, reshape(h, [1, ds]), 0);
    t = t + 1
  };
  out
}

def u:ssm_sel_decay(x, Wa, ba) {
  "The token-dependent decay [n, ds]: sigmoid(x Wa + ba), in (0, 1). The bias is what gives the decay a learnable baseline, so that Wa = 0 reproduces SS01's fixed decay exactly and the selective block contains the constant one as a special case; without it the decay starts at one half and the state loses half its content every position.";
  sigmoid(matmul(x, Wa) + ba)
}

def u:ssm_sel_gates(x, Wa, ba, Wb, Wc) {
  "The three token-dependent gates of the selective block as a record, for inspection and diagrams: decay a in (0, 1), input b = x Wb, and read c = x Wc, each [n, ds]. Traced code calls the pieces directly, because a record field access is not a traced form inside grad (finding F17).";
  {a: u:ssm_sel_decay(x, Wa, ba), b: matmul(x, Wb), c: matmul(x, Wc)}
}

def u:ssm_sel_states(x, Wa, ba, Wb, Wc, n, ds) {
  "The selective state at every position [n, ds]: the decay and input gates from the token, then the scan.";
  u:ssm_sel_scan(u:ssm_sel_decay(x, Wa, ba), matmul(x, Wb), n, ds)
}

def u:ssm_sel_out(x, Wa, ba, Wb, Wc, Wo, n, ds) {
  "The selective block output [n, dm]: every state read through its own token's gate c, then the output projection Wo; the caller adds the residual.";
  matmul(u:ssm_sel_scan(u:ssm_sel_decay(x, Wa, ba), matmul(x, Wb), n, ds) * matmul(x, Wc), Wo)
}

def u:ssm_sel_params(dm, ds) {
  "Trainable parameters of the selective block: three token-to-state projections, the decay bias, and one state-to-token projection.";
  3 * dm * ds + ds + ds * dm
}
